  "changes": [
    {
      "id": "F01",
      "before": "Its test-control predicate rejects an enabled run with no native spawn and a strict run with any delegation; reading this predicate is not running that control.",
      "after": "Its test-control predicate returns no refusal in mode `off`. In `on` or `strict`, zero native spawns are refused only when `expected || delegations > 0`; with `expected:false` and zero spawns/zero delegations it returns no refusal. A strict run with any delegation is refused. Reading this predicate is not running that control.",
      "source_refs": [
        "packages/core/src/omni.ts:139-153"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F02_F03",
      "before": "PTY sessions keep a bounded retained output ring and at most 25 exited sessions. `exact:true` uses supplied environment plus terminal defaults and adds no login argument; on Windows locale defaults are also added. Attachment returns replay/cursor before live activation. A replay gap sends terminal reset plus a cleaned first-line boundary and requests repaint. Inactive subscribers accumulate pending chunks until activation; synchronous callbacks and a bounded replay ring do not establish network backpressure. Teardown stops or explicitly adopts Omni descendants, and layer finalization waits only up to seven seconds for pending stops. The maintenance skill separately records the unresolved non-reading WebSocket client memory limit. [6,7]",
      "after": "PTY sessions keep a bounded retained output ring. Exited sessions enter an asynchronous `runFork` path that publishes the exit event before evicting the oldest entries while the retained count exceeds 25; this is an eviction policy, not an instantaneous upper bound. `exact:true` suppresses process-environment inheritance and automatic login arguments in the basic creation path; terminal defaults still apply, with locale defaults on Windows. Explicit `shellIntegration:true` can still invoke `ShellIntegration.prepare`, whose returned preparation can replace arguments and add environment entries. This qualifies the basic exact path without asserting the unread helper's internals. [6]\n\nAttachment returns replay/cursor before live activation. When retained output is replayed across a gap, it is prefixed with a terminal reset. `afterFirstLine` drops the prefix only when the first newline index is nonnegative and less than 4096; otherwise it retains the buffer. Repaint is requested during `activate()` only when there is a gap and the PTY session is still running. Inactive subscribers accumulate pending chunks until activation; synchronous callbacks and a bounded replay ring do not establish network backpressure or bound memory for a slow/non-reading WebSocket client. Teardown stops or explicitly adopts Omni descendants, and layer finalization waits only up to seven seconds for pending stops. The maintenance skill separately records that unresolved client-memory limit. [6,7,12]",
      "source_refs": [
        "packages/core/src/pty.ts:23-39,74-108,139-228,229-423,424-449",
        "packages/core/src/pty/protocol.ts:44-48",
        ".orchestra/skills/terminal-maintenance/SKILL.md:10-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F04",
      "before": "Source contracts about limits should be rechecked against the exact backend when runtime verification is needed.",
      "after": "Source contracts about limits should be rechecked against the exact backend when runtime verification is needed.\n\nThe terminal-maintenance skill prescribes that one PTY implementation serves both HTTP surfaces, the legacy handlers and `@orchestra/server`; changes must be coordinated across both. It also requires `bun run generate` from `packages/client` for a wire-protocol change. These are normative maintenance obligations from the skill, not execution evidence that both surfaces were exercised or client generation ran in this production. [7]",
      "source_refs": [
        ".orchestra/skills/terminal-maintenance/SKILL.md:10-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PTY_ANCHOR",
      "before": "- **6.** `packages/core/src/pty.ts:fc08cb64d832f77b145c4c9702d417d7db49c14f` — retention, exact creation, replay and teardown, lines 23–39,74–108,139–197,229–329,370–423.",
      "after": "- **6.** `packages/core/src/pty.ts:fc08cb64d832f77b145c4c9702d417d7db49c14f` — retention policy, exact/integration creation, activation, replay and teardown, lines 23–39,74–108,109–228,229–423,424–449.",
      "source_refs": [
        "packages/core/src/pty.ts"
      ]
    },
    {
